---- Changes since 2.660 ----
Added a "New updates are found" choice to the "Send email when" option that sends a complete report only when new updates become available, so notify-only schedules no longer repeat the same message every run.
---- Changes since 2.641 ----
Added a Held updates view with controls to hold, unhold or explicitly update APT-held packages.
---- Changes since 1.490 ----
First version of this module.
---- Changes since 1.500 ----
Debian backport versions are no longer falsely suggested for upgrading, if the apt-show-versions command is installed.
---- Changes since 1.790 ----
When updating multiple packages, they are done in a single YUM or APT operation if possible.
---- Changes since 1.900 ----
Added a tab for managing APT and YUM repos.
